    "Full API spec": "Public API and contracts\n\nModule: caro.errors\n- class InvalidMoveError(Exception): raised when a move is invalid while the game is IN_PROGRESS (e.g., out-of-bounds or cell occupied). Message must be informative but tests rely only on type.\n- class GameOverError(Exception): raised when attempting to move after the game has ended (win or draw). Tests rely on type.\n\nModule: caro.types\n- enum Player(Enum): X = 'X', O = 'O'. Stable identity and string representation not relied upon beyond enum equality.\n- enum Status(Enum): IN_PROGRESS = 'IN_PROGRESS', X_WON = 'X_WON', O_WON = 'O_WON', DRAW = 'DRAW'.\n\nModule: caro.move\n- @dataclass(frozen=True) class Move: row: int; col: int; player: Player. Immutable record appended to game history per successful move.\n\nModule: caro.board\n- class Board:\n  - __init__(self, size: int = 15): initialize square grid size x size with None cells; size must be >= 1.\n  - in_bounds(self, row: int, col: int) -> bool: returns True if 0 <= row < size and 0 <= col < size.\n  - get_cell(self, row: int, col: int) -> Player | None: returns occupant or None; requires in-bounds; callers ensure bounds.\n  - is_empty(self, row: int, col: int) -> bool: True if cell is None; requires in-bounds.\n  - set_cell(self, row: int, col: int, player: Player) -> None: sets cell to player; requires in-bounds and empty; engine enforces validations.\n  - is_full(self) -> bool: True if no None cells remain.\n  - to_matrix(self) -> list[list[Player | None]]: deep copy of grid for external observation.\n\nModule: caro.rules\n- def has_five_or_more(board: Board, row: int, col: int, player: Player) -> bool: Pure function; checks if placing player at (row, col) creates a contiguous line of length >= 5 in any of four directions: horizontal (0,1), vertical (1,0), diagonal down-right (1,1), diagonal up-right (-1,1). Counts include the placed stone; reads board via get_cell and in_bounds only; no mutations or side effects.\n\nModule: caro.game\n- class CaroGame:\n  - __init__(self, size: int = 15, first_player: Player = Player.X): creates Board(size), sets _first_player and _current_player, sets _status = Status.IN_PROGRESS, _winner = None, and empty _history.\n  - move(self, row: int, col: int) -> None: Validation order strictly enforced:\n    1) If status != IN_PROGRESS: raise GameOverError before any other check; history/state unchanged.\n    2) If not board.in_bounds(row, col): raise InvalidMoveError.\n    3) If not board.is_empty(row, col): raise InvalidMoveError.\n    On success: board.set_cell(row, col, _current_player), append Move(row, col, _current_player) to history; call rules.has_five_or_more; if True, set status to X_WON/O_WON accordingly, set _winner, and do not toggle player. Else, if board.is_full(): set status to DRAW; else toggle _current_player and leave status IN_PROGRESS.\n  - reset(self) -> None: reset board to empty, clear history, set status to IN_PROGRESS, set winner None, and restore _current_player to _first_player.\n  - board(self) -> list[list[Player | None]]: return Board.to_matrix() snapshot.\n  - current_player(self) -> Player: return current active player.\n  - status(self) -> Status: return current game status.\n  - winner(self) -> Player | None: return winner when status is X_WON or O_WON; else None.\n  - history(self) -> list[Move]: return a shallow copy or read-only view of history (tests will not mutate).\n\nModule: caro.__init__\n- Export symbols: CaroGame, Player, Status, Move, InvalidMoveError, GameOverError; do not execute code at import time beyond symbol binding.\n\nModule: Main\n- Behavior: Construct CaroGame(size=15, first_player=Player.X); execute the exact canonical nine-move sequence to achieve a horizontal X win on the ninth move; print a single status line (e.g., 'Status: X_WON') and exit. No loops beyond fixed sequence, no input, no randomness.\n\nImport direction constraints\n- caro/errors.py and caro/types.py are foundational and must not import from caro.game, caro.rules, or Main.\n- caro/rules.py imports only Board and Player (from caro.board and caro.types). It must not import CaroGame or Main.\n- caro/game.py may import Board, Move, Player, Status, and errors, as well as rules.has_five_or_more.\n- Main.py imports only from caro package; tests import Main and caro.* modules only.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "The project preserves protocol files requirements.txt, Main.py, and tests/test_main.py. The public API is exposed via caro/__init__.py and includes CaroGame, Player, Status, Move, InvalidMoveError, and GameOverError. The import graph is acyclic: errors/types/move/board are foundational, rules is pure, and game orchestrates. Main.py is a thin, deterministic bootstrap that constructs CaroGame, performs exactly nine moves, prints once, and exits. Tests are headless and deterministic; they import Main, caro, caro.errors, and caro.types only; no UI or I/O interactions beyond a single print in Main.py.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Run tests with: python -m pytest -q. There is exactly one protocol-level test file: tests/test_main.py. Runtime entrypoint is Main.py, which executes a canonical nine-move demo, prints a single status line, and exits. No manual interaction, network, or OS-dependent behavior is permitted. Additional files must not alter protocol files.",
    "Anything UNCLEAR": "Default board size is assumed to be 15 (consistent with the design). If a different default size is required for the canonical coordinates, please confirm."
}
